<title>FINLAND: Nokia rises sharply on Merrill upgrade.</title>
<headline>Nokia rises sharply on Merrill upgrade.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish telecommunications group Nokia Oy rose sharply on Wednesday, helped by a reaffirmed &quot;buy&quot; recommendation from U.S. investment house Merrill Lynch, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 1615/1315 GMT, Nokia traded at a life-high 363.00 markka, up 11.00 or more than three percent, in solid 200 million markka volume.</p>
<p>Brokers said both Nokia and Swedish rival Ericsson rose after Merrill Lynch had reaffirmed its &quot;buy&quot; on both groups.</p>
<p>--John Acher, Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 235</p>
</text>
